# Q.af dark mode context

Project: `/Users/0x/Desktop/q.af` (Next.js app in `app/` subdirectory)

## Files involved

- Root layout: `app/src/app/layout.tsx`
  - `<html lang="ar" dir="rtl">`
  - Uses `Cairo` Google font.
- Dashboard shell: `app/src/components/SidebarLayout.tsx`
  - Topbar class: `.topbar`
  - Actions container: `.topbar-actions`
  - Best place for toggle: next to `.topbar-create-btn` inside `.topbar-actions`.
- Dashboard styles: `app/src/app/dashboard.css`
  - Already dark-themed.
  - Tokens are scoped to `.app-body.app-root` and `body` overrides at the top of the file.
  - Shell classes: `.shell-grid`, `.sidebar-panel`, `.main-col`, `.topbar`, `.content-area`.
- Global light theme: `app/src/app/globals.css`
  - Light variables in `:root`.
  - Already has a `prefers-color-scheme: dark` media query near the end, but no class-based manual toggle.
- Orphaned inline styles: `app/src/lib/darkStyles.ts`
  - Exports React `CSSProperties` objects.
  - Unused in current components; do not treat as the active dark mode system.

## Token mapping (reuse from dashboard.css for global dark mode)

