html.dark {
  --bg: #061022;
  --bg-2: #0b1833;
  --paper: #0d1a38;
  --ink: #eef2ff;
  --muted: #9aa4b2;
  --muted-2: #6b7a94;
  --line: rgba(255, 255, 255, .08);
  --line-strong: rgba(255, 255, 255, .14);
  --background: #061022;
  --border: rgba(255, 255, 255, .09);
  --card: #0d1a38;
  --bg-elev: #0f1d40;
  --bg-card: #0d1a38;
  --text: #eef2ff;
}
```

## Notes

- `next-themes` was not installed in this project as of the session start.
- Lint (`npm run lint --quiet`) and typecheck (`npx tsc --noEmit`) passed before theme work began.
- The dashboard currently relies on hardcoded dark colors in `dashboard.css`, so the marketing pages are the main surfaces that need the new `html.dark` variables.
- Mobile: `.topbar-actions` collapses gracefully; keep the toggle small (icon-only) so it survives the 768px breakpoint.
